## What You've Learnt

After completing this lesson, you can:

- ✓ Read values from memory using LD A,(HL)
- ✓ Understand memory is both readable and writable
- ✓ Use CP instruction to compare values
- ✓ Understand CP sets flags without changing A
- ✓ Interpret Z flag (equality) and C flag (less-than)
- ✓ Use conditional jumps (JR Z, JR NZ)
- ✓ Implement read-compare-branch pattern
- ✓ Verify written data by reading it back
- ✓ Build foundation for collision detection
- ✓ Understand how games make decisions

**Key insight:** Reading + comparing + branching = intelligence. Your programme can now inspect the world and react to what it finds. This is the foundation of game logic.

**Next lesson:** Simple Repetition - Use DJNZ loops to draw multiple characters in a row. Combine character writing (lesson 3) with counted loops to create patterns. One step closer to drawing the snake body!

